### Day 13: Constructors
* **Daily Topics:** Default constructor, parameterized constructor, constructor overloading, `this` keyword.
* **Simple Explanations and Definitions:** A constructor is a special method used to initialize objects. It has the same name as the class and no return type.
* **Example and Code:**
```java
class Book {
    String title;
    int pages;

    // Parameterized constructor
    Book(String title, int pages) {
        this.title = title;
        this.pages = pages;
    }

    void display() {
        System.out.println(title + " has " + pages + " pages.");
    }
}

public class ConstructorDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Book myBook = new Book("Java Programming", 350);
        myBook.display();
    }
}
```
* **Coding Problems and Exercise:** Create a `Rectangle` class with default and parameterized constructors to calculate area.
* **Important Interview Questions:** What is the purpose of the `this` keyword in Java?
* **Revision and Practice tasks:** Implement constructor chaining using `this()`.

