### Day 29: File Handling
* **Daily Topics:** `File` class, reading files using `Scanner` or `BufferedReader`, writing files using `FileWriter` or `BufferedWriter`.
* **Simple Explanations and Definitions:** File handling allows reading from and writing to files stored on your disk system using standard Java I/O classes.
* **Example and Code:**
```java
import java.io.FileWriter;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.Scanner;
import java.io.File;

public class FileDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            // Writing to a file
            FileWriter writer = new FileWriter("test.txt");
            writer.write("Hello from File Handling!");
            writer.close();

            // Reading from a file
            File file = new File("test.txt");
            Scanner scanner = new Scanner(file);
            while (scanner.hasNextLine()) {
                System.out.println(scanner.nextLine());
            }
            scanner.close();
        } catch (IOException e) {
            System.out.println("An error occurred.");
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```
